  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mozambique - ACJR 2023 (Joint Budget)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUMMARY
The Mozambique Joint Response 2023, responding to the needs that have arisen in the aftermath of the Freddy cyclone, will be implemented through a consortium led by Plan International and additionally consists of CAREm Oxfam, Save the Children, SOS, Tearfund and locals partners: CCM, AENA, NANA, FH, KULIMA and ADRA. The joint budget is allocated by the Mozambique  Joint Response partners. The joint budget is set aside to facilitate regional meetings, joint activities, travel and communication costs, real time review and the salary of the Mozambique Joint Response in-country Coordinator. The budget is managed by Plan International in its role as MOZ JR lead.</narrative>
  </description>
